Nothing makes sense no more.

1675
01:27:18,790 --> 01:27:20,150
I truly miss the old days, you know.

1676
01:27:20,310 --> 01:27:21,970
Back when we actually got along.

1677
01:27:22,370 --> 01:27:24,170
Building that marvel of engineering together.

1678
01:27:24,650 --> 01:27:25,510
That was something.

1679
01:27:26,030 --> 01:27:27,170
Wasn't easy, let me tell you.

1680
01:27:27,310 --> 01:27:28,390
I could've done it alone.

1681
01:27:28,390 --> 01:27:30,270
Took us months to get it balanced right.

1682
01:27:30,750 --> 01:27:32,150
One wrong valve, and boom!

1683
01:27:32,690 --> 01:27:33,510
Backyard waterfall.

1684
01:27:34,170 --> 01:27:36,690
Imagine what we could've built if we'd kept that piece.

1685
01:27:37,490 --> 01:27:38,830
Real innovation, real change.

1686
01:27:39,710 --> 01:27:44,910
Now, thanks to snacks, drunks, escapades, and harebrained ideas, the key's stuck in that damn balloon!

1687
01:27:45,350 --> 01:27:48,070
We had real momentum, real tech, and now we're stuck in the mud.

1688
01:27:49,550 --> 01:27:51,810
I ain't hurt the sweet whir of machinery in years.

1689
01:27:54,960 --> 01:27:56,780
You got a nice hang instrument there.

1690
01:27:58,980 --> 01:28:01,320
Uh, where- have you seen The Out Llama?

1691
01:28:04,550 --> 01:28:05,750
Out Llama Steakhouse.

1692
01:28:07,130 --> 01:28:10,930
Dear Diary, I started the day feeling more nervous than usual.

1693
01:28:11,830 --> 01:28:16,050
Onkly woke me up by knocking on my door, saying they had something to show me.

1694
01:28:16,730 --> 01:28:18,070
Oh, what do I do?

1695
01:28:18,650 --> 01:28:24,910
I told them, doing my best to sound irritated, that people really shouldn't go around disturbing others while they're working in their home.

1696
01:28:25,470 --> 01:28:28,610
That next time, they should just leave a note, and I'll come when I can.

1697
01:28:29,170 --> 01:28:32,570
They just laughed, slid a tiny piece of paper under my door, and walked away.

1698
01:28:33,370 --> 01:28:34,490
Oh, that laugh.

1699
01:28:34,970 --> 01:28:37,750
Well, at least it gave me time to apply my best varnish.

1700
01:28:38,210 --> 01:28:39,470
I wonder if they noticed.

1701
01:28:39,990 --> 01:28:41,190
Should I bring those flowers?

1702
01:28:41,350 --> 01:28:44,270
Those incredible rare alliums I found a couple of days ago.

1703
01:28:44,670 --> 01:28:47,170
It cost me so much to get them, and I know why I did it.

1704
01:28:47,690 --> 01:28:48,410
Who they are for.

1705
01:28:49,550 --> 01:28:50,850
Nuh-uh, back to the drawer.

1706
01:28:51,350 --> 01:28:53,670
Anyway, the note only said observatory.

1707
01:28:54,110 --> 01:28:57,050
So I climbed up to that new place where Uncle Bob is working.

1708
01:28:57,670 --> 01:29:02,430
There they said they needed a pair of strong, rugged arms to operate a piece of machinery.

1709
01:29:02,430 --> 01:29:02,810
Heh.

1710
01:29:03,690 --> 01:29:06,490
They said it was to finish assembling something called the Stellarium.

1711
01:29:07,110 --> 01:29:08,630
They showed me a small prototype.

1712
01:29:09,170 --> 01:29:11,610
Something that runs on holograms, or something of the sort.

1713
01:29:12,130 --> 01:29:14,610
They also showed me experiments on fire propulsion.

1714
01:29:15,170 --> 01:29:16,810
Which they told me is a secret for now.

1715
01:29:17,350 --> 01:29:20,670
I don't quite understand those things, it's not my field, but uh...

1716
01:29:20,670 --> 01:29:21,070
Oh my.

1717
01:29:21,290 --> 01:29:24,810
How beautiful it is to see how passionately they speak about their work.

1718
01:29:25,290 --> 01:29:29,930
I could spend entire days just listening to them and watching them light up about those nerdy little wonders.

1719
01:29:29,930 --> 01:29:35,050
I swear, I even noticed their upper eye gleamed brighter than the others while they explained.

1720
01:29:35,550 --> 01:29:37,010
The day couldn't have ended better.

1721
01:29:37,410 --> 01:29:40,330
After all that hard work, they said they didn't know how to thank me.

1722
01:29:40,630 --> 01:29:42,150
I told them we are a community.

1723
01:29:42,390 --> 01:29:46,390
And that there's nothing more gratifying than seeing your peers thrive in what they love.

1724
01:29:46,810 --> 01:29:48,210
I think they liked hearing that.

1725
01:29:48,810 --> 01:29:53,570
The thing is, just as we were leaving, right outside the observatory, there was a table set up.

1726
01:29:54,030 --> 01:29:56,150
Fully served with moss truffles.

1727
01:29:56,490 --> 01:29:57,310
My favorite.

1728
01:29:58,030 --> 01:29:59,110
My goodness, sir.

1729
01:29:59,350 --> 01:30:00,570
I wonder how they knew.

1730
01:30:01,070 --> 01:30:03,070
There were also candles lighting the place.

1731
01:30:03,450 --> 01:30:06,130
If only they knew, how much those scare me.

1732
01:30:06,410 --> 01:30:08,050
But I guess they didn't look bad.

1733
01:30:08,050 --> 01:30:08,990
It was... fine.

1734
01:30:09,430 --> 01:30:10,630
The food was exquisite.

1735
01:30:10,950 --> 01:30:12,790
And the conversation, even more so.

1736
01:30:13,210 --> 01:30:15,910
They asked me to tell them more about my views on community.

1737
01:30:15,910 --> 01:30:19,090
I shared how fascinated I am by the way we live.

1738
01:30:19,750 --> 01:30:25,170
Cooperating with one another, never using our talents as an advantage to step over someone, or leave anyone behind.

1739
01:30:25,650 --> 01:30:29,190
How beautiful it is to constantly reach out and hold each other's hands.

1740
01:30:29,770 --> 01:30:33,810
We conform a collective with different goals, each individual part with its own desires.

1741
01:30:34,310 --> 01:30:36,770
Yet we all understand we are nothing without each other.

1742
01:30:36,770 --> 01:30:41,050
I feel like our roots are entwined around the same shared heart.

1743
01:30:42,550 --> 01:30:44,690
I wouldn't trade our village for anything in the world.

1744
01:30:45,150 --> 01:30:46,630
Well, maybe for one thing.

1745
01:30:46,890 --> 01:30:48,290
But I wouldn't say that out loud.

1746
01:30:48,770 --> 01:30:51,950
What Unkel said next is what truly undid me.

1747
01:30:52,570 --> 01:30:58,610
You know, behind that hard chipped mozzy bark, there's a tender wood the world needs and deserves to see.

1748
01:30:59,050 --> 01:31:01,230
I saw your lower eye glow so brightly.

1749
01:31:01,590 --> 01:31:04,950
I think I could help send down those rough edges a little, don't you think?

1750
01:31:05,490 --> 01:31:06,450
Oh, sand them down?

1751
01:31:06,790 --> 01:31:08,510
Oh my god, I got so nervous.

1752
01:31:08,690 --> 01:31:10,170
I wish I had my blindfolds.

1753
01:31:10,290 --> 01:31:12,770
Maybe that way they could have got closer and closer to me.

1754
01:31:13,330 --> 01:31:15,590
And I would give them the whole power over my being.

1755
01:31:16,290 --> 01:31:21,310
To be at their complete mercy that they don't stop looking at me, that they forces me to remain absolutely still and...

1756
01:31:21,750 --> 01:31:23,950
Naturally, I told them I was sick of their shitty jokes.

1757
01:31:24,390 --> 01:31:27,330
They laughed, turned away, and then sat gazing up at the sky.

1758
01:31:27,850 --> 01:31:29,030
That thing about the roots?

1759
01:31:29,170 --> 01:31:30,230
It's a beautiful thought, you know.

1760
01:31:30,530 --> 01:31:31,810
And you're absolutely right.

1761
01:31:32,270 --> 01:31:35,610
But haven't you ever wondered how high our branches could reach if we really tried?

1762
01:31:36,270 --> 01:31:37,330
Good night, comrade.

1763
01:31:37,990 --> 01:31:39,410
I don't know what to think.

1764
01:31:39,730 --> 01:31:40,850
Their upper eye?

1765
01:31:41,030 --> 01:31:41,790
My lower one?

1766
01:31:42,410 --> 01:31:43,530
Is this really happening?

1767
01:31:44,210 --> 01:31:45,090
Nah, no way.

1768
01:31:45,210 --> 01:31:45,910
I'm too old for this.

1769
01:31:46,390 --> 01:31:47,730
I've already had my moments.

1770
01:31:47,730 --> 01:31:49,310
Since my train has already passed.

1771
01:31:49,850 --> 01:31:50,510
Who am I kidding?

1772
01:31:50,970 --> 01:31:54,790
I need to focus all my attention on refining the final adjustments of the sluice system.

1773
01:31:55,250 --> 01:31:56,830
There's no point in showing feelings.

1774
01:31:57,270 --> 01:31:58,830
Feelings are... cringe.

1775
01:31:59,470 --> 01:32:00,030
Cringe?

1776
01:32:00,770 --> 01:32:02,410
Did I seriously use that word?

1777
01:32:03,090 --> 01:32:03,630
Ugh!

1778
01:32:03,870 --> 01:32:04,870
What's wrong with me?

1779
01:32:05,030 --> 01:32:06,390
I sound like a teenager.

1780
01:32:06,850 --> 01:32:08,490
Almost like a sapling.

1781
01:32:08,730 --> 01:32:09,410
A hatchling.

1782
01:32:09,770 --> 01:32:10,870
A frickin'...

1783
01:32:10,870 --> 01:32:11,790
Yeah.

1784
01:32:16,460 --> 01:32:17,400
Nicely done, sir.

1785
01:32:18,760 --> 01:32:19,240
Um...

1786
01:32:19,240 --> 01:32:20,200
What did you tell me?

1787
01:32:21,860 --> 01:32:23,520
He likes to get drunk, this guy, huh?

1788
01:32:24,460 --> 01:32:24,940
Okay.

1789
01:32:25,880 --> 01:32:27,200
The key stuck in the balloon.

1790
01:32:29,240 --> 01:32:29,720
Hmm...

1791
01:32:29,720 --> 01:32:30,220
Damn.

1792
01:32:33,670 --> 01:32:34,150
Well...

1793
01:32:34,150 --> 01:32:35,690
Oh, something about balancing things.

1794
01:32:36,690 --> 01:32:37,510
What did you say?

1795
01:32:38,730 --> 01:32:39,210
Right.

1796
01:32:41,190 --> 01:32:43,830
Well, I think I may have to utilize this.

1797
01:32:47,050 --> 01:32:48,450
Yes!

1798
01:32:51,010 --> 01:32:52,170
Easy!

1799
01:32:53,570 --> 01:32:54,330
Ooh!

1800
01:32:59,310 --> 01:33:00,150
Tanax Balloon!

1801
01:33:00,370 --> 01:33:00,830
Cargo...

1802
01:33:00,830 --> 01:33:02,910
You know what I mean?

1803
01:33:03,810 --> 01:33:04,510
Below.

1804
01:33:06,370 --> 01:33:07,070
Huh.

1805
01:33:16,000 --> 01:33:16,900
Okay.

1806
01:33:20,440 --> 01:33:21,380
Where's the key?

1807
01:33:22,460 --> 01:33:23,240
No!

1808
01:33:24,000 --> 01:33:25,420
Okay, we can't take fall damage.

1809
01:33:25,700 --> 01:33:26,160
Thank God.

1810
01:33:26,880 --> 01:33:27,380
Let me try that again.

1811
01:33:29,480 --> 01:33:30,140
Take me!

1812
01:33:30,840 --> 01:33:31,360
Go!

1813
01:33:33,040 --> 01:33:33,560
Whee!

1814
01:33:34,440 --> 01:33:34,960
Whoa!

1815
01:33:36,640 --> 01:33:37,160
Oof!

1816
01:33:42,820 --> 01:33:43,720
Oh, that was scary!

1817
01:33:44,700 --> 01:33:45,660
Didn't like that.

1818
01:33:46,240 --> 01:33:47,360
There's no key up here.

1819
01:33:47,420 --> 01:33:48,280
What are you talking about?

1820
01:33:49,440 --> 01:33:51,300
The key's stuck in that damn balloon!

1821
01:33:53,600 --> 01:33:54,120
Hmm...

1822
01:33:54,620 --> 01:33:55,700
I need a key here.

1823
01:33:58,480 --> 01:33:59,300
Oh, wait, wait, wait.

1824
01:34:03,140 --> 01:34:03,940
Load balancing.

1825
01:34:07,600 --> 01:34:07,880
Yeah!

1826
01:34:08,040 --> 01:34:08,280
No!

1827
01:34:09,420 --> 01:34:10,040
Oh, no.

1828
01:34:12,800 --> 01:34:13,640
Oh, wait a minute.

1829
01:34:13,680 --> 01:34:14,200
Is that a telescope?

1830
01:34:15,660 --> 01:34:16,300
That's neat.

1831
01:34:19,320 --> 01:34:19,720
Yeah!

1832
01:34:19,920 --> 01:34:20,180
Crap.

1833
01:34:21,240 --> 01:34:22,140
Can I get up here?

1834
01:34:23,860 --> 01:34:24,940
Oh, my God!

1835
01:34:25,180 --> 01:34:26,120
Look at this staircase!

1836
01:34:28,960 --> 01:34:30,260
That is amazing!

1837
01:34:31,580 --> 01:34:32,900
I'm in awe of this!

1838
01:34:35,180 --> 01:34:36,120
How on earth...

1839
01:34:37,560 --> 01:34:38,760
That is beautiful.

1840
01:34:41,940 --> 01:34:42,780
Intercom's ventures?

1841
01:34:42,980 --> 01:34:43,360
Oh, my God.

1842
01:34:43,460 --> 01:34:44,500
That's just like...

1843
01:34:44,500 --> 01:34:45,680
Oh, wait, I can't use it.

1844
01:34:47,380 --> 01:34:48,760
Do I see a key from here?

1845
01:34:58,600 --> 01:35:00,040
Went on an adventure today.

1846
01:35:00,040 --> 01:35:00,660
It was fun.

1847
01:35:01,480 --> 01:35:04,040
We ventured through the jungle, found some wild animals.

1848
01:35:04,400 --> 01:35:05,940
Also saw some beavers on a dam.

1849
01:35:06,420 --> 01:35:08,500
Made me think, what if we also build a dam?

1850
01:35:09,680 --> 01:35:10,600
New adventure today.

1851
01:35:10,960 --> 01:35:12,520
Went into the cave together with Iceboo.

1852
01:35:13,100 --> 01:35:14,700
Spoke to them about that dam idea.

1853
01:35:15,160 --> 01:35:18,520
They said we could build it right there before the big pit the water flows into.

1854
01:35:19,100 --> 01:35:22,080
It would make the waterfall down there a hell of a lot more spectacular.

1855
01:35:23,160 --> 01:35:23,960
Another adventure.

1856
01:35:23,960 --> 01:35:25,720
Went by Saidiulp.

1857
01:35:26,200 --> 01:35:26,920
Spoke about the dam.

1858
01:35:27,460 --> 01:35:29,020
They also think it's a great idea.

1859
01:35:29,580 --> 01:35:33,220
Mentioned we could place a sluice into it to control the water level in the village.

1860
01:35:33,320 --> 01:35:34,400
That's what a sluice is!

1861
01:35:34,960 --> 01:35:35,880
I get it now.

1862
01:35:36,300 --> 01:35:37,840
I think this is a good plan.

1863
01:35:38,140 --> 01:35:40,880
Although I think a hole plugger would work way better.

1864
01:35:41,640 --> 01:35:42,940
Isn't that just called a plug?

1865
01:35:43,820 --> 01:35:45,400
This week was very adventurous.

1866
01:35:45,740 --> 01:35:46,800
We built the dam.

1867
01:35:47,400 --> 01:35:48,940
The sluice system works great.

1868
01:35:49,240 --> 01:35:51,800
The whole lower part of the village can be flooded on command.

1869
01:35:52,200 --> 01:35:52,680
What?!

1870
01:35:53,100 --> 01:35:53,840
I'm gonna do that.

1871
01:35:54,060 --> 01:35:54,760
I'm gonna flood everyone.

1872
01:35:54,900 --> 01:35:55,400
Everyone dies.

1873
01:35:56,120 --> 01:35:57,740
Uncle Bob was the first to try it out.

1874
01:35:59,000 --> 01:36:01,720
To ensure safety, we cut off the power to the sluice system.

1875
01:36:02,120 --> 01:36:04,000
Don't want the place to flood on accident, you know?

1876
01:36:05,180 --> 01:36:05,540
Right.

1877
01:36:06,440 --> 01:36:08,920
Saidiulp is the owner of the keycard to the sluice power room.

1878
01:36:09,260 --> 01:36:10,460
They swore to keep it safe.

1879
01:36:10,460 --> 01:36:11,020
I trust them.

1880
01:36:12,200 --> 01:36:13,880
Had an amazing time with Saidiulp today.

1881
01:36:14,300 --> 01:36:15,960
We went flying in my hot air balloon.

1882
01:36:16,120 --> 01:36:16,900
It was so fun.

1883
01:36:17,220 --> 01:36:19,280
They did manage to leave their keycard in there though.

1884
01:36:19,280 --> 01:36:20,660
Blame me for it.

1885
01:36:21,120 --> 01:36:22,780
We'll probably go and get it tomorrow.

1886
01:36:24,200 --> 01:36:24,620
Really.

1887
01:36:25,140 --> 01:36:26,420
Not an adventure today.

1888
01:36:27,060 --> 01:36:30,980
Sadly, our village elder and good friend Uncle Bob appears to have passed away this morning.

1889
01:36:31,220 --> 01:36:31,900
We're all in shock.

1890
01:36:32,720 --> 01:36:35,060
Sitting here looking over the village, I feel empty inside.

1891
01:36:35,940 --> 01:36:38,600
It's been a while since I've been up here looking over the village.

1892
01:36:39,040 --> 01:36:40,520
Haven't talked to the others in weeks.

1893
01:36:41,040 --> 01:36:42,720
Everyone seems annoyed at each other.

1894
01:36:43,460 --> 01:36:45,260
Saidiulp is still mad over that keycard.

1895
01:36:45,600 --> 01:36:46,740
It's still up there.

1896
01:36:47,260 --> 01:36:48,040
Is it though?

1897
01:36:48,040 --> 01:36:48,660
I just checked.

1898
01:36:49,200 --> 01:36:51,880
This will probably be my last time on the lookout platform.

1899
01:36:52,320 --> 01:36:54,620
Can't stand walking by Saidiulp's house anymore.

1900
01:36:55,040 --> 01:36:56,320
All they do is yell at me.

1901
01:36:57,080 --> 01:36:58,380
Iceboo isn't much better either.

1902
01:36:58,680 --> 01:37:03,060
They've been drinking a lot and telling us that it's our fault Uncle Bob has passed away.

1903
01:37:04,400 --> 01:37:04,880
Really?

1904
01:37:05,800 --> 01:37:06,400
Haha!

1905
01:37:06,960 --> 01:37:07,880
Look at those fuckers...

1906
01:37:09,460 --> 01:37:10,060
houses...

1907
01:37:11,000 --> 01:37:14,120
I'm gonna burn them fuck down when I get out again.

1908
01:37:14,740 --> 01:37:17,000
First let me drink the rest of this bottle.

1909
01:37:18,480 --> 01:37:19,080
Iceboo!

1910
01:37:19,460 --> 01:37:21,120
I'm coming for your ass!

1911
01:37:21,780 --> 01:37:23,280
Your ass is mine!

1912
01:37:24,380 --> 01:37:25,560
No more drinking.

1913
01:37:26,340 --> 01:37:27,940
No burning down villages.

1914
01:37:28,780 --> 01:37:30,100
Only flooding villages.

1915
01:37:30,100 --> 01:37:30,900
And that's what I do.

1916
01:37:31,900 --> 01:37:33,640
I will actually flood this village.

1917
01:37:34,880 --> 01:37:35,660
So we gotta...

1918
01:37:35,660 --> 01:37:37,100
So apparently there's a key up there.

1919
01:37:40,350 --> 01:37:41,530
I'm not seeing a key.

1920
01:37:41,710 --> 01:37:42,110
Let me try again.

1921
01:37:43,150 --> 01:37:43,850
Take me!

1922
01:37:47,960 --> 01:37:48,500
Swoop!

1923
01:37:49,880 --> 01:37:50,420
Whoa!

1924
01:37:52,880 --> 01:37:53,920
Okay, so hold on.

1925
01:37:54,700 --> 01:37:55,720
I go in here.

1926
01:37:57,940 --> 01:37:59,740
Am I seeing something down there?

1927
01:38:15,480 --> 01:38:16,560
Uh, charge...

1928
01:38:16,560 --> 01:38:18,520
No, cargo hanging below.

1929
01:38:22,840 --> 01:38:23,280
Huh.

1930
01:38:29,250 --> 01:38:30,190
Heh heh heh.

1931
01:38:30,830 --> 01:38:31,370
Oh god.

1932
01:38:32,710 --> 01:38:33,150
Oof!

1933
01:38:34,270 --> 01:38:34,810
Oh wait!

1934
01:38:34,870 --> 01:38:35,410
Something over there!

1935
01:38:36,630 --> 01:38:37,770
I think I found something.

1936
01:38:43,210 --> 01:38:43,650
Yeah!

1937
01:38:43,850 --> 01:38:45,650
Sluice controls power room key card!

