The sun.

2205
01:51:33,250 --> 01:51:34,090
Let's read about the sun.

2206
01:51:34,750 --> 01:51:39,370
Yeah, our sun is awesome, I get it, but there are other types of stars that are much cooler.

2207
01:51:40,290 --> 01:51:40,930
You're right.

2208
01:51:41,510 --> 01:51:41,990
Technically.

2209
01:51:42,810 --> 01:51:45,390
I'm finally starting to understand the nature of pulsars.

2210
01:51:45,390 --> 01:51:52,670
So it seems they pop into existence when a neutron star spins so fast that gravity just, you know, flips into magnetism.

2211
01:51:52,990 --> 01:51:54,630
Like, who knew spinning could do that?

2212
01:51:55,250 --> 01:51:57,090
Magnetic field of a pulsar is nuts.

2213
01:51:57,490 --> 01:52:00,470
It's apparently so strong it keeps all the neutrons from decaying.

2214
01:52:00,650 --> 01:52:03,970
Like, the neutrons are just chilling, safe inside their little magnetic bubble.

2215
01:52:04,530 --> 01:52:04,970
Yeah.

2216
01:52:05,310 --> 01:52:08,470
And if there's a very huge magnetic field, they also have a very fun name.

2217
01:52:09,110 --> 01:52:10,770
That sounds a lot like magnet.

2218
01:52:11,370 --> 01:52:17,690
If a pulsar spins faster than a thousand times per second, it's gonna collapse into a black hole from centrifugal pressure.

2219
01:52:18,130 --> 01:52:19,590
That sounds wild, I mean.

2220
01:52:19,970 --> 01:52:23,890
Physics is basically a party trick sometimes when you don't understand them, but now I do.

2221
01:52:25,230 --> 01:52:25,670
Yeah.

2222
01:52:26,670 --> 01:52:27,810
And here's the kicker.

2223
01:52:27,890 --> 01:52:32,550
We could, in theory, use the rhythm of a pulsar to figure out how fast the universe is expanding.

2224
01:52:32,550 --> 01:52:34,610
because space stretches the beats.

2225
01:52:34,970 --> 01:52:45,070
So by listening carefully to a pulsar's beat, advanced civilizations can measure the quantum heartbeat of the universe itself, because each pulse is subtly distorted by dark matter fluctuations.

2226
01:52:45,530 --> 01:52:46,890
This is something else.

2227
01:52:47,210 --> 01:52:50,170
I will say, though, it's beautifully written.

2228
01:52:51,170 --> 01:52:52,670
I enjoy reading it.

2229
01:52:54,050 --> 01:52:54,690
Exit!

2230
01:52:56,070 --> 01:52:57,150
Uh, hold on.

2231
01:52:57,550 --> 01:52:57,930
Oh!

2232
01:53:02,630 --> 01:53:04,730
Uncle Bob's bread for experimenting.

2233
01:53:05,390 --> 01:53:07,170
Why do humans even eat this?

2234
01:53:09,050 --> 01:53:10,390
Wait, this is...

2235
01:53:11,450 --> 01:53:12,490
Rat bread!

2236
01:53:15,550 --> 01:53:16,850
I don't like that.

2237
01:53:17,390 --> 01:53:18,810
I don't want rat bread.

2238
01:53:19,810 --> 01:53:21,140
Wait, how is this even...

2239
01:53:24,430 --> 01:53:25,130
Huh.

2240
01:53:25,450 --> 01:53:25,950
Okay.

2241
01:53:28,390 --> 01:53:29,370
Down we go.

2242
01:53:31,450 --> 01:53:32,150
Cheers.

2243
01:53:37,300 --> 01:53:37,740
Okay.

2244
01:53:38,920 --> 01:53:40,220
We head further down now.

2245
01:53:41,480 --> 01:53:43,460
I want to see what's at the end of the sluice.

2246
01:53:49,060 --> 01:53:49,860
It's a grate!

2247
01:53:54,340 --> 01:53:55,440
Ooh, that's far down.

2248
01:53:56,280 --> 01:53:57,400
Can I not go down there?

2249
01:54:00,770 --> 01:54:01,530
All right, then.

2250
01:54:01,710 --> 01:54:02,810
Let's go check out the village.

2251
01:54:04,050 --> 01:54:04,910
See what happened.

2252
01:54:08,690 --> 01:54:10,130
Well, the water level is higher.

2253
01:54:13,350 --> 01:54:14,590
Oh, there's a boat!

2254
01:54:21,490 --> 01:54:23,350
Someone played the drums just now.

2255
01:54:27,600 --> 01:54:28,280
Uh...

2256
01:54:29,880 --> 01:54:31,200
That's kind of creepy.

2257
01:54:32,460 --> 01:54:33,640
What's up, guys?

2258
01:54:35,720 --> 01:54:36,780
It's Tnak.

2259
01:54:38,100 --> 01:54:38,900
Saidiope and...

2260
01:54:38,900 --> 01:54:39,600
Iceby.

2261
01:54:40,720 --> 01:54:41,440
Oh, oh!

2262
01:54:41,720 --> 01:54:42,620
I didn't mean to do that.

2263
01:54:43,340 --> 01:54:44,020
Up we go.

2264
01:54:45,480 --> 01:54:46,880
Holy crap, that was intense.

2265
01:54:47,140 --> 01:54:48,500
Thought I was gonna drown again, but nope!

2266
01:54:49,000 --> 01:54:51,780
Turns out we just dove head first into reconnecting with each other.

2267
01:54:53,120 --> 01:54:53,780
That's what I do.

2268
01:54:53,860 --> 01:54:54,560
I bring people together.

2269
01:54:54,780 --> 01:54:57,980
I can't wait to get back to doing all kinds of crazy stuff with my old pals.

2270
01:54:58,000 --> 01:55:00,940
This time, you know, with some responsible consideration or...

2271
01:55:01,480 --> 01:55:01,880
Whatever.

2272
01:55:03,360 --> 01:55:03,800
Okay.

2273
01:55:05,240 --> 01:55:07,340
The mess you caused, kid, I gotta admit.

2274
01:55:07,600 --> 01:55:08,840
I think I'm glad it happened.

2275
01:55:09,340 --> 01:55:11,060
Turns out my neighbors aren't the fools I thought.

2276
01:55:11,360 --> 01:55:13,960
They've got some damn fine brains on their shoulders when trouble hits.

2277
01:55:15,660 --> 01:55:16,540
Playing the guitar!

2278
01:55:17,360 --> 01:55:18,560
High blind were we, huh?

2279
01:55:19,140 --> 01:55:21,000
We even like the same blasted song.

2280
01:55:21,140 --> 01:55:22,100
Feels like we're a team again.

2281
01:55:22,740 --> 01:55:24,580
Almost like Uncle Bob's here with us somehow.

2282
01:55:26,080 --> 01:55:27,540
Yeah, this Uncle Bob guy...

2283
01:55:27,540 --> 01:55:28,420
Or something else.

2284
01:55:29,820 --> 01:55:31,000
Reminds me of someone else.

2285
01:55:32,340 --> 01:55:32,760
Ice...

2286
01:55:33,900 --> 01:55:35,500
Oh my gosh, what have you done?

2287
01:55:36,020 --> 01:55:37,280
This is delightful.

2288
01:55:38,000 --> 01:55:41,680
We just went through a horrible mess, but it forced us to come together with a common goal.

2289
01:55:42,060 --> 01:55:42,970
And now we realize...

2290
01:55:44,180 --> 01:55:45,820
Just how much we actually have in common.

2291
01:55:46,480 --> 01:55:49,060
You can bet your boots were getting absolutely plastered tonight.

2292
01:55:49,500 --> 01:55:51,800
Sharing old stories, playing some good old tunes.

2293
01:55:52,200 --> 01:55:54,000
And lighting up a proper bonfire together.

2294
01:55:54,600 --> 01:55:58,600
And hey, if a house or two catches a fire, maybe it's just the warmth we needed.

2295
01:55:58,600 --> 01:56:00,900
Dude, they're all playing their instruments!

2296
01:56:02,100 --> 01:56:02,880
Guitar!

2297
01:56:03,360 --> 01:56:04,320
Hang glider!

2298
01:56:04,640 --> 01:56:05,480
And piano!

2299
01:56:06,160 --> 01:56:06,980
What the fuck?

2300
01:56:10,480 --> 01:56:11,840
Beautiful ode here.

2301
01:56:12,240 --> 01:56:13,060
Well done, guys.

2302
01:56:13,380 --> 01:56:14,480
That's beautiful.

2303
01:56:15,200 --> 01:56:16,280
Very nice.

2304
01:56:17,480 --> 01:56:18,620
Very nice.

2305
01:56:21,600 --> 01:56:23,320
Looks like my job is done here.

2306
01:56:23,440 --> 01:56:24,680
Friendships were brought together.

2307
01:56:24,820 --> 01:56:25,000
But!

2308
01:56:26,100 --> 01:56:26,920
Where's the llama?

2309
01:56:28,520 --> 01:56:30,000
One of these is the llama.

2310
01:56:31,920 --> 01:56:32,440
Maybe.

2311
01:56:36,120 --> 01:56:37,180
It's dripping honey.

2312
01:56:40,060 --> 01:56:41,720
It's a nice song you got going there.

2313
01:56:42,340 --> 01:56:43,040
Let me go over here.

2314
01:56:46,560 --> 01:56:47,860
Oh, that was Tnak's home.

2315
01:56:47,960 --> 01:56:48,140
Okay.

2316
01:56:49,640 --> 01:56:50,520
Sluice Axis.

2317
01:56:51,000 --> 01:56:53,180
I was wondering where that guy was, but he was over here.

2318
01:56:53,300 --> 01:56:53,440
Okay.

2319
01:56:54,200 --> 01:56:54,920
It makes sense.

2320
01:56:56,840 --> 01:56:58,140
But where is this llama?

2321
01:57:00,060 --> 01:57:02,900
The little kid wrote that the llama was here.

2322
01:57:04,600 --> 01:57:05,120
Somewhere.

2323
01:57:07,040 --> 01:57:08,740
That's a small slice of cake.

2324
01:57:13,840 --> 01:57:14,700
Thrillseeker thoughts.

2325
01:57:15,080 --> 01:57:15,940
Ooh, that's a long one.

2326
01:57:16,940 --> 01:57:17,760
That's Tnak.

2327
01:57:18,480 --> 01:57:19,680
That was awesome.

2328
01:57:19,880 --> 01:57:22,200
I should totally go rafting blindfolded more often.

2329
01:57:22,620 --> 01:57:25,320
Pretty sure death gave me a friendly little pat on the back there.

2330
01:57:25,920 --> 01:57:28,420
Chillest brush with mortality yet, bro.

2331
01:57:29,580 --> 01:57:31,500
The way your senses kick into overdrive.

2332
01:57:31,580 --> 01:57:34,400
The way you feel the world when you just let go and trust the ride.

2333
01:57:34,740 --> 01:57:35,600
It's next level.

2334
01:57:36,140 --> 01:57:36,660
It's okay.

2335
01:57:36,660 --> 01:57:37,520
We brought them together.

2336
01:57:37,700 --> 01:57:40,820
We don't need to understand why they got apart.

2337
01:57:41,180 --> 01:57:43,040
All that matters is their friends right now.

2338
01:57:43,900 --> 01:57:45,400
This is a good ending to this.

2339
01:57:46,540 --> 01:57:47,600
I'm gonna go up here now.

2340
01:57:47,720 --> 01:57:48,720
Because I want to find this llama.

2341
01:57:50,080 --> 01:57:51,840
We need a lot of llamas here.

2342
01:57:52,620 --> 01:57:53,020
Four.

2343
01:57:53,180 --> 01:57:53,560
Oh!

2344
01:57:55,680 --> 01:57:56,580
Look at that.

2345
01:57:56,720 --> 01:57:59,880
It's inspecting the butt of a moss cruncher.

2346
01:58:02,790 --> 01:58:04,090
Oh, nice sounds.

2347
01:58:09,530 --> 01:58:10,270
Wait a minute.

2348
01:58:22,120 --> 01:58:22,960
That's a cannon.

2349
01:58:26,800 --> 01:58:27,740
What's happening here?

2350
01:58:31,060 --> 01:58:32,020
Hey, our llama!

2351
01:58:32,740 --> 01:58:34,720
Wanna come over and help me out of the mine?

2352
01:58:35,500 --> 01:58:36,220
Nah, man.

2353
01:58:36,360 --> 01:58:37,340
I'm busy right now.

2354
01:58:37,920 --> 01:58:40,740
You see, I think the skeleton here used to be a whale in distant past.

2355
01:58:42,340 --> 01:58:44,600
It must have washed ashore due to these horrible tides.

2356
01:58:46,080 --> 01:58:49,760
Now, I've been doing some research and I think that damn moon is the culprit.

2357
01:58:51,260 --> 01:58:51,660
Really?

2358
01:58:52,120 --> 01:58:52,600
You know?

2359
01:58:52,940 --> 01:58:54,640
That bastard that shows up every night?

2360
01:58:55,260 --> 01:58:56,060
I think...

2361
01:58:56,060 --> 01:58:57,520
I think I'm gonna blow it up.

2362
01:58:57,800 --> 01:58:58,200
Yeah!

2363
01:58:58,960 --> 01:59:00,400
I have my TNT cannon ready.

2364
01:59:00,820 --> 01:59:03,520
Now I just need the exact coordinates of the moon so I don't miss.

2365
01:59:05,000 --> 01:59:05,360
Nice.

2366
01:59:05,660 --> 01:59:06,700
You got the coordinates of the moon.

2367
01:59:06,780 --> 01:59:07,180
I got it!

2368
01:59:07,280 --> 01:59:07,400
Yeah!

2369
01:59:08,120 --> 01:59:10,420
Come back at night and we'll blow that bastard out of the moon up.

2370
01:59:12,040 --> 01:59:12,400
Hmm.

2371
01:59:14,240 --> 01:59:15,700
Will you then come with me?

2372
01:59:16,960 --> 01:59:18,040
I'm assuming you will.

2373
01:59:18,240 --> 01:59:19,100
What the...

2374
01:59:19,800 --> 01:59:20,540
Hold on a minute.

2375
01:59:21,180 --> 01:59:21,520
No!

2376
01:59:22,340 --> 01:59:23,020
Back out, back out!

2377
01:59:27,350 --> 01:59:28,950
Ooh, the beeping intensified.

2378
01:59:31,740 --> 01:59:32,680
What's happening up there?

2379
01:59:34,200 --> 01:59:35,440
Oh look, that's the telescope.

2380
01:59:36,240 --> 01:59:36,980
That's amazing.

2381
01:59:38,140 --> 01:59:39,120
That's so cool!

2382
01:59:42,590 --> 01:59:44,030
Oh, we can advance time, right?

2383
01:59:45,270 --> 01:59:46,770
But maybe we can't do that anymore.

2384
01:59:47,610 --> 01:59:48,870
Since I now have done this.

2385
01:59:50,610 --> 01:59:51,170
Let's see.

2386
01:59:57,880 --> 01:59:58,960
Uh, maybe over here.

2387
02:00:01,100 --> 02:00:02,640
There was something over here, wasn't there?

2388
02:00:10,950 --> 02:00:11,710
Uncle Bob!

2389
02:00:15,640 --> 02:00:16,580
I guess I could...

2390
02:00:16,580 --> 02:00:18,020
What happens if I put the sluice back?

2391
02:00:19,000 --> 02:00:20,120
Can I change it again?

2392
02:00:21,440 --> 02:00:23,960
I wanna try this, just because I'm curious now.

2393
02:00:26,920 --> 02:00:28,780
I don't wanna leave you guys flooded forever.

2394
02:00:29,880 --> 02:00:31,220
I'm glad I brought you together.

2395
02:00:31,220 --> 02:00:33,520
Now you can, uh, you know, go back to your houses.

2396
02:00:34,600 --> 02:00:35,780
No more water damage.

2397
02:00:36,760 --> 02:00:37,660
I will fix it.

2398
02:00:41,820 --> 02:00:42,760
Can't leave you stranded.

2399
02:00:50,070 --> 02:00:51,090
Oh, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

2400
02:00:51,270 --> 02:00:53,110
Oh, I probably can't bring it back up.

2401
02:00:54,750 --> 02:00:55,930
Yeah, the power's off.

2402
02:00:56,090 --> 02:00:56,570
Right, okay.

2403
02:00:58,630 --> 02:00:59,550
So I go over here.

2404
02:01:01,410 --> 02:01:02,150
Turn it on.

2405
02:01:04,430 --> 02:01:05,670
And I'll bring this back up.

2406
02:01:08,010 --> 02:01:09,670
Would be kinda mean to leave it flooded, right?

2407
02:01:12,110 --> 02:01:12,430
Damn!

2408
02:01:17,180 --> 02:01:18,120
I mean, that's what it is.

2409
02:01:18,240 --> 02:01:18,760
It's a dam.

2410
02:01:21,340 --> 02:01:22,480
Alright, back we go.

2411
02:01:23,220 --> 02:01:24,340
We gotta wait till night.

2412
02:01:27,380 --> 02:01:29,200
It's so weirdly quiet in this boat.

2413
02:01:32,160 --> 02:01:34,620
It's like a slight, uh, floating Voldemort here.

2414
02:01:36,020 --> 02:01:37,240
I don't know how I like that.

2415
02:01:38,920 --> 02:01:39,720
Literally unplayable.

2416
02:01:40,800 --> 02:01:41,480
Let's go up here.

2417
02:01:44,320 --> 02:01:46,460
Uh, I also want to...

2418
02:01:46,460 --> 02:01:47,640
go to Funland.

2419
02:01:48,360 --> 02:01:49,720
But for that we need the...

2420
02:01:49,720 --> 02:01:50,280
thingy, right?

2421
02:01:50,380 --> 02:01:50,860
Let me see here.

2422
02:01:53,420 --> 02:01:55,720
We need five shingles to mingle with Sarah Reddust.

2423
02:01:56,120 --> 02:01:57,220
Yeah, I don't have that yet.

2424
02:01:57,320 --> 02:01:58,220
We gotta earn money somehow.

2425
02:01:58,720 --> 02:02:00,280
Funland shop contains stuff for enter.

2426
02:02:01,040 --> 02:02:01,440
Right.

2427
02:02:03,360 --> 02:02:04,100
Let's do that.

2428
02:02:06,080 --> 02:02:08,320
So we know the location of one of the llamas.

2429
02:02:08,560 --> 02:02:09,400
What is that?

2430
02:02:14,330 --> 02:02:15,610
What am I looking at?

2431
02:02:17,310 --> 02:02:17,870
Sir?

2432
02:02:19,690 --> 02:02:20,250
Rosenfeld!

2433
02:02:21,350 --> 02:02:22,390
Ah, I see.

2434
02:02:23,330 --> 02:02:26,310
Another tourist appreciating my beautiful tulip field.

2435
02:02:27,350 --> 02:02:29,530
I've had this field for over 50 years.

2436
02:02:29,950 --> 02:02:32,130
I've been growing more and more flowers every year.

2437
02:02:32,910 --> 02:02:33,850
You know what?

2438
02:02:33,990 --> 02:02:35,950
I even cancelled my insurance last week.

2439
02:02:36,810 --> 02:02:37,350
Why?

2440
02:02:38,030 --> 02:02:40,630
Yeah, nothing will touch my lovely tulip field.

2441
02:02:40,850 --> 02:02:42,150
It will be with me forever.

2442
02:02:43,530 --> 02:02:47,110
It would be a shame if someone were to set fire to everything, wouldn't it now?

2443
02:02:48,530 --> 02:02:48,950
Hmm.

2444
02:02:50,610 --> 02:02:52,270
It would be a real shame.

2445
02:02:56,330 --> 02:02:56,750
Hey.

2446
02:02:57,470 --> 02:02:58,130
I'm back.

2447
02:02:58,990 --> 02:03:00,450
I'm going into Agni's house.

2448
02:03:00,630 --> 02:03:01,090
Don't tell her.

2449
02:03:02,130 --> 02:03:03,410
Oh shit, Agni, I'm sorry.

2450
02:03:04,590 --> 02:03:05,910
I'm here to fix your TV.

2451
02:03:06,890 --> 02:03:07,910
It's upstairs, right?

2452
02:03:08,090 --> 02:03:08,210
Yeah.

2453
02:03:08,590 --> 02:03:09,330
It's upstairs.

2454
02:03:11,850 --> 02:03:13,370
There in Bag Aegean.

2455
02:03:14,030 --> 02:03:15,090
Today was a good day.

2456
02:03:15,230 --> 02:03:19,030
I woke up with renewed strength after a long and arduous journey to the deep.

2457
02:03:19,630 --> 02:03:22,530
I got so many diamonds, lots of iron and other things.

2458
02:03:22,910 --> 02:03:24,050
Made it back safely.

2459
02:03:24,050 --> 02:03:24,770
Almost.

2460
02:03:25,050 --> 02:03:28,390
I decided to sail over a ridge and got stuck down below.

2461
02:03:28,750 --> 02:03:29,590
Sad times.

2462
02:03:30,090 --> 02:03:31,050
I made it home.

2463
02:03:31,630 --> 02:03:33,910
I remember where this happened.

2464
02:03:35,050 --> 02:03:37,170
I got chased by demons in the sky.

2465
02:03:37,170 --> 02:03:38,630
Whoa, Agni's.

2466
02:03:40,570 --> 02:03:42,250
Didn't realize you were standing there.

2467
02:03:43,430 --> 02:03:44,690
I am sorry.

2468
02:03:45,210 --> 02:03:46,330
I'll be out of your hair.

2469
02:03:47,410 --> 02:03:49,010
I guess this is Agni's child.

2470
02:03:51,550 --> 02:03:54,310
If this is Agni, this is Agni.

2471
02:03:56,950 --> 02:03:58,210
Okay, this one's for sale.

